---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const seo = {
  title: "How to Track Mutual Funds Across Multiple AMCs in India | Arthavi",
  description: "Learn how to track mutual fund schemes from HDFC, SBI, ICICI, Nippon, Quant, and others in one place using CAS statements and Arthavi.",
};

const schema = JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  "headline": seo.title,
  "description": seo.description,
  "datePublished": "2026-11-09",
  "author": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "Arthavi Editorial Team" }
});
---
<Layout
  title={seo.title}
  description={seo.description}
  keywords="track mutual funds multiple amcs india, all amc tracker, mutual fund consolidation"
  schema={schema}
  breadcrumb={{
    items: [
      { name: "Home", url: "https://arthavi.com/" },
      { name: "Blog", url: "https://arthavi.com/blog/" },
      { name: "Track Mutual Funds Across AMCs", url: "https://arthavi.com/blog/track-mutual-funds-multiple-amcs/" }
    ]
  }}
>

<main class="container" style="padding-top: calc(var(--header-height) + 2rem); padding-bottom: 5rem;">
  <article class="prose fade-in" style="max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto;">
    <h1>How to Track Mutual Funds Across Multiple AMCs in India</h1>
    <p class="text-muted" style="font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.7;">
      The average Indian mutual fund investor holds between 6 and 14 schemes spread across 4 to 8 different Asset Management Companies (AMCs). Logging into each fund house website is tedious and leaves you without a consolidated XIRR.
    </p>

    <h2>The Power of the Consolidated Account Statement (CAS)</h2>
    <p>
      SEBI mandates two primary Registrar and Transfer Agents (RTAs) in India: CAMS and KFintech. Together, they service 100% of the mutual fund industry. A single CAS PDF generated from CAMS or KFintech contains every single transaction, folio, unit balance, and current valuation associated with your PAN.
    </p>

    <h2>How Arthavi Merges Statements Seamlessly</h2>
    <p>
      Arthavi's multi-CAS reconciliation engine is built specifically for Indian investors:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Upload statements from both CAMS and KFintech without conflict.</li>
      <li>Reconcile personal and work email folios tied to the same PAN.</li>
      <li>Use <strong>CAS Delta Import</strong> to update monthly records without duplicating past transactions.</li>
      <li>Get an instant <strong>AMC Concentration Chart</strong> highlighting whether you are over-exposed to a single fund management house.</li>
    </ul>

    <div style="text-align: center; margin: 3rem 0;">
      <a href="https://app.arthavi.com/register" class="btn btn-primary" style="padding: 1rem 2.5rem; font-size: 1.1rem; margin-right: 1rem;">Consolidate Your Mutual Funds</a>
      <a href="https://app.arthavi.com/demo" class="btn btn-demo" style="padding: 1rem 2.5rem; font-size: 1.1rem;">Try Demo</a>
    </div>

  </article>
</main>

</Layout>
